    {
      "id": "8a4ebb39-b1d3-47f1-8f57-235d4377e9c9",
      "name": "Sticky Status Guard",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        688,
        336
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Status guard\n\nBlocks all writes when the ticket is already `solved` or `closed`.\n\nAdded after 2026-07-23: Zendesk redelivered a `ticket created` webhook 8h37m late, the automation re-ran on the original email and contradicted its own earlier reply.\n\nUses the base `status` string, so no `cs_project_config` column is needed and `closed` is covered for free.\n\nSafe for legitimate follow-ups: Zendesk auto-reopens a solved ticket on requester reply, so status is `open` by the time the 2nd-message flow calls this.",
        "height": 260,
        "width": 460,
        "color": 3
      }
    }
